GitHub Actions Runner Modernization

This one has the strongest before/after story — deprecated tooling is an easy risk narrative.

Metrics to pull:

Job queue wait time p50/p95 — ARC exports this to Prometheus; for the "before," pull historical runs via gh api /repos/{owner}/{repo}/actions/runs and diff created_at vs run_started_at
Repos / workflows / teams migrated
Peak concurrent runners and scale-to-zero behavior
Runner image: CVE count before vs. after, patch cadence (ad-hoc → nightly/weekly), image build time
Compute cost delta (Cost Explorer filtered on the runner node group tag)
Hours/month of manual runner maintenance eliminated
CI incidents attributable to runner failures, before vs. after

Phrasing:

Migrated [N] self-hosted runners off an unsupported Summerwind deployment to Actions Runner Controller scale sets, covering [N] repos and [N] teams with zero unplanned CI downtime during cutover. Automated runner image builds moved patching from ad-hoc to [cadence], cutting base image critical/high CVEs from [N] to [N]. Scale-to-zero reduced runner compute spend [X]% ($[N]/mo), and p95 job queue time dropped from [N]s to [N]s.
